WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.461
What if an AI could not only tell you where a
street photo was taken,

00:00:04.541 --> 00:00:06.040
but explain how it knew?

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.277
This paper introduces GeoReasoner,

00:00:08.357 --> 00:00:14.134
a large vision-language model for street-view
geo-localization that reasons like a human.

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:20.452
The authors tackle two long-standing obstacles:
street-view training data is full of low-quality

00:00:20.532 --> 00:00:22.294
images with no visual clues,

00:00:22.374 --> 00:00:27.164
and existing localization models are black boxes
that give no explanation.

00:00:27.244 --> 00:00:31.573
GeoReasoner solves both by quantifying how
locatable each image is,

00:00:31.653 --> 00:00:36.114
borrowing human inference knowledge from real
geo-localization games,

00:00:36.194 --> 00:00:38.746
and fine-tuning in two dedicated stages.

00:00:38.826 --> 00:00:44.603
The result beats comparable vision-language models
by over twenty-five percent at country

00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:47.564
level and thirty-eight percent at city level,

00:00:47.644 --> 00:00:51.710
while matching a specialist trained on fifteen
times more data.
